  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A function is surjective, when the range of the function is same as the co-domain.</p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#160;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8746;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
